    2. Pick 1-3 mover shapes (area 4-10, bbox 2-5h x 2-4w, 4-connected).
    3. Place movers at grid bottom (bbox bottom = row N-1), separated by >=1 bg column, no overlap. This is the output position.
    4. Pick 1-2 marker shapes (area 1-3, 4-connected). Place markers in upper rows, not overlapping any drop path columns or final mover positions.
    5. Compute input by lifting each mover upward by a random offset (ensuring all stay within grid, row 0 stays bg, and enough empty rows exist below for the drop to be non-trivial).
